                                "sense_id": "fbc0e0a7-7da1-3f56-aec6-0c846765bc7d",
                                "text": "“[…] if I am questioned, I shall merely say that I designed it myself, with a little assistance from a professional architect, whose intentions were good, but who had never been called upon to live in a house of his own planning. Will that answer?” / \"“Perfectly,” replied Mr. Brook; “it will amply account for the—well, we will say the unprofessionalness of the plan.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "751b96f9-e4c2-4bb1-bd9e-5d7851bde77c",
                                "sense_id": "fbc0e0a7-7da1-3f56-aec6-0c846765bc7d",
                                "text": "Lethaby was enchanted by the gaiety, by the casualness, by the unprofessionalness (in the qualifications, frock-coat sense) of the Rossetti, Morris, Webb, Burne-Jones set."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cc48c93-1628-4857-8365-a5522c8e1bed",
                                "sense_id": "fbc0e0a7-7da1-3f56-aec6-0c846765bc7d",
                                "text": "Psychology has unanimously affirmed that the more practice situations resemble use situations, the better the learning will function in the use situations. Ignoring so fundamental a principle only impedes mastery and attests to slovenly unprofessionalness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
